    "blurb": "Orchestrate Databricks data and AI",
    "overview": "Orchestrate the Databricks Data Intelligence Platform from BPMN with 15 operations across SQL Statement Execution, SQL warehouses, Jobs, Model Serving, and Vector Search. Authenticate with an OAuth service principal and run it on the Camunda Connectors Bundle.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Orchestrate Databricks SQL, Jobs, and AI models",
    "splashDescription": "Call the Databricks Data Intelligence Platform directly from a BPMN process, instead of writing custom integration code for each API you need. The Connector covers 15 operations across five Databricks APIs: SQL Statement Execution, SQL warehouses, Jobs, Model Serving, and Vector Search. Select a Databricks API, then an operation, and the Connector derives the endpoint path, HTTP method, and query parameters for you. Configure a single workspace URL, and the OAuth token endpoint is derived from it, with authentication handled through OAuth machine-to-machine using a service principal, or a personal access token for testing. Because it's built on Camunda's REST protocol Connector, there is no custom runtime, JAR, or self-managed worker to deploy, and SQL values are passed as bound statement parameters rather than concatenated into the statement. Long-running work stays visible in the process model: trigger a Databricks job or SQL statement, then poll for its terminal state with a timer and an exclusive gateway, so waiting is interruptible and auditable.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/865363/overview/img14848506874856550755.png?ec27e466a5721abf60375eed4a53b891",
    "imageSrcset": {
      "default": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/865363/overview/img14848506874856550755.png",
